  "sampling": "Exactly 16 fresh-process samples per fixed lane, 48 total in user_1_1 then user_8_1 then user_1_0 order. Four same-ELF A/A pairs cover both subjects/scales, followed by two reversed comparison blocks per scale. 50000 sends after 5000 warmup. Three short instrumentation smoke samples excluded. No extension based on results.",
  "analysis": "Two descriptive block ratios per scale/lane; no confidence or equivalence claim. Retain all counters and daemon/caller/total CPU and wall, including adverse values.",
  "decision": "Proceed toward physical-router performance only when the primary user_8_1 lane has median instructions/op <= -3% against R124 at both 0/64 held scales, with every same-ELF instruction A/A pair in all three lanes within +/-0.5%. user_1_1 and user_1_0 are regression observations, not required to improve 3%. Any primary screen failure stops this candidate; no new controls/variants without attribution. These are resource-allocation heuristics, not necessary conditions for performance benefit or a language-limit proof. CPU/op is not latency.",
  "boundaries": "Enable ACK after warmup before the three clock reads; disable ACK after the loop and the three clock reads. No per-request instrumentation. Final callback validates delivery; bounded trailing daemon work can straddle the CPU-clock/disable boundary. Counts include this boundary overhead and are divided by 50000.",
